ine: a novel approach to the treatment of type 2 diabetes</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2000</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1154</fpage><lpage>1161</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10937514</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22-dmso-3-043"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aminorroaya</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Janghorbani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramezani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Haghighi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Amini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does bromocriptine improve glycemic control of obese type-2 diabetics?</article-title><source>Horm Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15205563</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b23-dmso-3-043"><label>23</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamath</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Yip</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of a quick-release form of bromocriptine (Ergoset) on fasting and postprandial plasma glucose, insulin, lipid, and lipoprotein concentrations in obese nondiabetic hyperinsulinemic women</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>1997</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1697</fpage><lpage>1701</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9353611</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b24-dmso-3-043"><label>24</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cincotta</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><sur